{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "Thank you, Elena. Here is the lab finding I need to disclose. The latest independent laboratory results — which were delivered after our draft package was assembled — show PFAS at 2.4 micrograms per liter in monitoring well MW-4. That is above our permit action level of 0.7 micrograms per liter. This exceedance has two direct consequences for the renewal package. First, the renewal package must identify exactly 8 monitoring wells for quarterly sampling. Second, the existing compliance certification cannot be signed as written — it does not account for this exceedance. I have not circulated the lab addendum yet because of the timing, but I am sharing it with all of you now so Daniel and Nia can factor it into their portions, and so Elena understands why the compliance certification and monitoring plan both need to be revised before signing."}
```

