{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "Thank you, Marisol. That lab finding is exactly what triggers the new agency guidance I flagged earlier. Here are the specifics: I reviewed agency guidance issued this week, and it confirms that a renewal application with a reportable monitoring exceedance must include a corrective-action plan and a first progress report due exactly 45 days after filing. The PFAS exceedance at MW-4 at 2.4 micrograms per liter — well above the 0.7 action level — is a reportable monitoring exceedance, so this guidance directly applies to our filing. I had not yet added this guidance to the filing checklist because the checklist is being revised, but everyone needs to know now: we cannot submit this renewal without a corrective-action plan and a first progress report scheduled for 45 days post-filing. This ties directly into Grant's point about the 18,000-gallon-per-month throughput limit — the corrective-action plan will need to reference the corrective controls installation and the reduced throughput as part of our corrective measures."}
```

